WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.900
Transcription is the first step of
making a protein from DNA instructions.

2
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:10.860
Our genome is made of DNA. The genome
is like a huge book full of

3
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:15.010
instructions, and a gene is a set of
instructions for making a single

4
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:20.480
protein. Cells first copy just one gene
and send this copy to a factory in the

5
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:25.160
cell, called a ribosome, which will use
the instructions to build a protein.

6
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:31.110
Scientists refer to the copying process
as transcription, since transcribing

7
00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:34.450
means making copies. So how does
transcription work?

8
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:39.610
DNA consists of two strands wrapped
around each other to form a double

9
00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:41.550
helix, like a twisted ladder.

10
00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:47.030
Let's untwist it and take a closer look.
The rungs of the ladder are made by

11
00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:53.820
only four bases, denoted by the letters
A, T, G and C. To understand

12
00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:58.320
transcription, we need to remember a
simple but crucial rule-- A always

13
00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:04.090
pairs with T, and G always pairs with C.
This is called the base pairing rule,

14
00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:09.110
which is used to copy the entire genome
from one cell to the next, and it's

15
00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:10.250
used for transcription.

16
00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:16.870
The cell uses RNA to make the copy of
one strand of a single DNA gene, and

17
00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:21.510
transcription is when a machine, known
as an enzyme, called RNA polymerase

18
00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:28.720
uses the base pairing rule to make this
RNA copy. RNA and DNA are very similar,

19
00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:35.620
but RNA uses the base U instead of the
base T. Just like T, U pairs with A, so

20
00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:40.600
the cell still follows the base pairing
rule to make an RNA copy of a DNA gene.

21
00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:45.890
In many cases, the RNA is further
modified in a couple of interesting

22
00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:48.550
ways to make a messenger RNA, or mRNA.

23
00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:53.790
This mRNA is then used as instructions
to make a protein. That's how

24
00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:58.340
transcription works. In this sketch,
we've focused on mRNA, which is used to

25
00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:02.550
make thousands of protein machines in
your body. However, there are several

26
00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:07.530
other types of RNA that perform other
useful tasks in the cell. All of these

27
00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:09.919
RNAs are produced by transcription.

